The  utility  uncompresses  files  compressed by and recompresses
them with The options are as follows: Overwrite  existing  files.
Unless  this  option  is specified, refuses to overwrite existing
files.  Test integrity of the gzipped file  before  deleting  the
original  file.   If the integrity check fails, the original file
is not removed.  Print a report specifying the achieved  compres‐
sion  ratios.  Use the ‐9 mode of achieving better compression at
the cost of slower execution.  Keep the original file if it  uses
less  disk  blocks  than  the  gzipped one.  A disk block is 1024
bytes.  The utility tries to maintain the file mode of the origi‐
nal file.  If the original file is not writable, it is  not  able
to do that and will print a warning.
